## METHOD BEING FOLLOWED (inherited from Pinterest build — proven to work)

1. Understand content supply first (audit real content) before platform
   strategy.
2. Test the smallest real unit before scaling to a full system.
3. Fix root causes with standing rules, not one-off patches.
4. Lock order: **content pool → format → volume/cadence → platform-specific
   mechanics → wording** — never start with caption wording.
5. Research each platform's actual current safe volume/frequency and
   algorithm behavior before fixing any daily number — never guess.
6. Verify any generated/sorted data file programmatically (counts, dupes,
   gaps) before presenting it as final — never eyeball large lists.
7. Confirm ambiguous volume/cadence instructions back to the operator before
   building on them.
8. When operator gives real source material (links, screenshots, actual site
   content), use it directly — never substitute invented/generic content.
9. Match the operator's preferred lean, low-filler communication style
   (confirmed explicitly in this thread: short, precise, step-by-step, no
   recaps, no walls of text, separate copy-paste boxes per output field).

