### Facebook SEO / per-post spec (researched, locked)

Facebook ranking = page metadata + keyword-aligned captions + early
engagement (shares/saves > comments > likes) + native-format content
(Reels > Video > Image > Text > Link). Native uploads only — cross-posted/
watermarked content gets suppressed. Facebook now surfaces public posts in
Google search too, so captions double as light SEO copy.

| Format | Caption length | Hashtags | Alt text | Link |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Nail image/carousel | 40–80 chars, punchy | 3–5, **specific to that day's actual design/topic, never generic** | Yes — real description of the specific nail design shown (not AI's generic auto-suggestion) | None |
| Website + link | 80–150 chars, hook included | 2–3, specific to topic | Not required (link preview auto-pulls site's own meta) | Yes, native auto-preview |
| Infographic+BGM video | 40–80 chars, written to match real search intent/query phrasing (e.g. "fall nails 2026" style, matches how the website's own blog titles are already phrased) | 3–5, specific to topic | No manual alt-text field exists for video on FB — caption + accurate cover/thumbnail frame is the practical equivalent | None |

Hashtags must always be pulled from the actual day's specific nail
design/topic — never generic filler tags like #beauty.

**Output format requirement (operator explicit correction):** Each field —
Caption, Hashtags, Alt text, Link — goes in its **own separate copy-paste
box**, clearly labeled outside the box. Do NOT merge everything into one
